{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I [A]got a gal at the head of the creek,
Go [A]up to see her 'bout the [E]middle of the [A]week,
[A]Kiss her on the mouth just as [D]sweet as any wine,
Wraps [A]herself around me like a [E]sweet potato [A]vine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Goin' up Cripple Creek, goin' in a run,
[A]Goin' up Cripple Creek to [E]have a little [A]fun,
[A]Goin' up Cripple Creek, goin' in a whirl,
[A]Goin' up Cripple Creek to [E]see my [A]girl.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[A]Cripple Creek's wide and Cripple Creek's deep,
I'll [A]wade old Cripple Creek be[E]fore I [A]sleep,
[A]Roll my breeches [D]to my knees,
I'll [A]wade old Cripple Creek [E]when I [A]please.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: A}
